I've identified the improvement. Here's the plan:

**Improvement: Add billing/quota error detection to diagnose_api_error and prevent wasteful retries of non-retriable billing errors in is_retriable_error**

Currently:
• Billing/quota exhaustion errors (e.g., Anthropic's "credit balance is too low", OpenAI's "insufficient_quota", "billing_hard_limit_reached") get NO diagnostic message — users just see a raw API error.
• Worse, some billing errors contain words like "capacity" or "limit" that match retriable patterns, causing up to 5 wasteful retry attempts that will all fail.
• Rate limit (429) errors are correctly retried but get no user-facing diagnostic explaining what's happening.

The fix:
1. Add billing/quota patterns to is_retriable_error's non-retriable list
2. Add billing/quota and rate-limit diagnosis to diagnose_api_error
3. Add comprehensive tests
